---
import { hero } from '../content/copy'

/**
 * The live-DOM agent view this hero defers to is scoped to a follow-up task
 * (plan batch 4). This ships the problem-claim headline and subhead the
 * groundwork operator picked, without the animated fixture.
 */
---

<section
  id="top"
  class="page-display flex min-h-[80vh] flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 px-6 text-center"
>
  {
    /* The headline takes the same column every other section uses. Capped
      narrower than the page it introduces, it wrapped a line further than it
      needed to, and the monospace family the page settled on is wider per
      character than the proportional one this width was chosen against. */
  }
  <h1
    class="max-w-4xl text-[length:var(--type-page-display-size)] leading-[var(--type-page-display-lh)] font-bold tracking-[-0.01em] text-(--color-text)"
  >
    {hero.headline}
  </h1>
  <p
    class="max-w-xl text-[length:var(--type-heading-size)] leading-[var(--type-heading-lh)] text-(--color-text-secondary)"
  >
    {hero.subhead}
  </p>
  <a href="#install" class="btn btn-primary">
    {hero.cta}
  </a>
</section>

<style>
  /*
   * The headline speaks in the page's own family.
   *
   * Measured over the whole page, the proportional family appeared exactly
   * once in 216 text elements, and one element in a family nothing else uses
   * is what read as belonging to another design. The same fault had already
   * been found and fixed on the primary button without anyone noticing the
   * headline carried it too.
   *
   * The size still comes from the display step, so the hero keeps its scale
   * and only its voice changes. Giving the interface a proportional voice
   * throughout, with mono kept for what is literally code, is a different and
   * larger decision that this one does not take.
   *
   * A prior cut set the family on the section rather than the heading, and it
   * cascaded into the subhead and the call to action, leaving the two primary
   * buttons on the page in two different typefaces.
   */
  .page-display > h1 {
    font-family: var(--type-body-family);
  }
</style>
